<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n94834" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκῐᾱμᾰχ-ία</span></b> , ἡ,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>a fighting against a
			shadow</i>: esp. <i>a form of exercise with hands and feet</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.153
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph.,
				<i>fighting with a shadow, mock-fight, 'beating the air</i>',
				<i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Fam.</u>
				11.14.1
			</span></i> (pl.), <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.514d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				663.16
			</span></i>; title of satire by Varro, Non.<i><span class="en">
				p.190
			</span></i> L.—<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκιομαχία</span></b>  is a later form, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				6.146
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
